Article 5 The tax basis for stamp tax is as follows:
(1) for taxable contracts, the tax basis shall be the amount stated in the contract, excluding the stated value-added tax amount;
(2) for taxable documents of title transfer, the tax basis shall be the amount stated in the document of title transfer, excluding the stated value-added tax amount;
(3) for taxable account books of business, the tax basis shall be the total amount of paid-in capital (share capital) and capital surplus recorded in the account books;
(4) for securities trading, the tax basis shall be the transaction amount.

Article 12 The following instruments shall be exempted from stamp tax:
(1) duplicates or copies of taxable instruments;
(2) taxable instruments executed by foreign embassies, consulates and representative offices of international organizations in China for obtaining premises, which shall be exempted from tax according to legal provisions;
(3) taxable instruments executed by the Chinese People's Liberation Army and the Chinese People's Armed Police Force;
(4) purchase and sale contracts and agricultural insurance contracts executed by farmers, family farms, specialized farmer cooperatives, rural collective economic organizations, and villagers committees for the purchase of agricultural production materials or the sale of agricultural products;
(5) interest-free or discounted loan contracts, and loan contracts executed by international financial organizations for providing preferential loans to China;
(6) documents of title transfer executed by property owners for donating property to the government, schools, social welfare institutions, or charitable organizations;
(7) purchase and sale contracts executed by non-profit medical and health institutions for the procurement of pharmaceuticals or medical materials;
(8) electronic orders concluded between individuals and e-commerce operators.
According to the needs of national economic and social development, the State Council may prescribe reduction or exemption of stamp tax for circumstances such as ensuring residents' housing needs, enterprise restructuring and reorganization, bankruptcy, and supporting the development of small and micro enterprises, and shall report to the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress for recordation.
